From b8d91bec753eaf2616ee44d7c23720830e45a344 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:32:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 087/108] gpu: vulkan_depth_4x_as_1x (off); library precompile
 marker covers the translation switches

vulkan_depth_4x_as_1x draws a 4x depth-only draw into a depth surface never drawn
with color into the 1x surface its samples form (surface info rewritten for the
draw, viewport/scissor/extent/point size/polygon offset scale doubled). Idea from
Xendroid+. In Lightning Returns' Ark view the shadow maps' 4x <-> 1x transfers
disappear, but other depth transfers into the same surfaces take their place:
12.08 -> 12.22 Mcycles per frame, so it stays off.

The pipeline library precompile marker now includes spirv_texture_sign_branch,
vulkan_shader_xenos_multiply(_vertex) and vulkan_texture_fetch_implicit_lod (version
3): changing translation rebuilds the libraries in the first-boot background pass
instead of compiling them during play.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

